<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB says Swiss gold revaluation a one-off.</title>
<headline>SNB says Swiss gold revaluation a one-off.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's proposed revaluation of official gold reserves would be a one-off measure for a long time to come, Swiss National Bank (SNB) chairman Hans Meyer was quoted as saying on Monday.</p>
<p>Meyer was interviewed by the newspaper Basler Zeitung about a joint SNB-government proposal to raise the valuation of gold reserves in line with higher market prices.</p>
<p>&quot;The cautious revaluation of gold stocks is a one-of-a-kind measure for a long time to come,&quot; Meyer said without elaborating.</p>
</text>
